# florilegium — .gitignore

# --- Source PDFs are copyright: NO source PDF in the repo, examples included.
#     Examples point at a DOI / open-access URL and are reproduced locally. ---
*.pdf

# --- Private planning docs (kept local, never published) ---
GUIDA_PUBBLICAZIONE.md
PROJECT_INVENTORY.md
CLAUDE.md
HANDOFF.md
MAPPATURA_NOMI_PRIVATA.md

# --- Private working material: NEVER publishable ---
#     Convention: any top-level directory whose name starts with an underscore holds
#     private working material — working copies of the source chain, pre-release review
#     reports, drafts. Ignored wholesale so that no `git add -A` can ever sweep them
#     into the public repository. Nothing published here depends on them.
_*/

# --- OS / editor junk ---
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
*~
.idea/
.vscode/

# --- Python runtime junk ---
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
venv/

# --- Local env / secrets ---
.env
.env.*
*.local

# --- Temp files ---
#     NOTE: no blanket *.lock here, on purpose. It would silently swallow
#     dependency lockfiles (uv.lock, poetry.lock, package-lock.json,
#     Cargo.lock), which MUST be tracked for reproducibility. When the engine
#     starts writing runtime locks, ignore them by their specific path.
*.tmp

# --- First Loop scratch renders (scripts/first_loop.py) ---
.florilegium-run-*/
